{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand corrections applied on top of the OCR pass by tools/build_coords.py.",
    "Positions are in pixels of .build/a18/drawing_full.png (5810 x 3420) so they",
    "can be checked against a crop of that file; the builder normalises them.",
    "",
    "Every test point is placed here rather than taken from OCR, because a test",
    "point's marker has to sit on the pad you actually probe, not on the text",
    "beside it. TP1-TP22 run in one row along the top edge, each label followed",
    "about 50 px to its right by the short bar that is the wire-loop pad, so the",
    "marker is centred between the two and sized to cover both. Positions were",
    "read directly off the drawing at 3-4x zoom; the row order left to right is",
    "TP4 TP2 TP5 TP11 TP13 TP8 TP19 TP21 TP20 TP17 TP18 TP3 TP1 TP6 TP16 TP15",
    "TP12 TP10 TP7 TP9, then TP14 (its label pushed up by the board notch), TP22",
    "and TP203."
  ],
  "imageSize": { "w": 5810, "h": 3420 },
  "_layersComment": [
    "Alignment of the photograph to board space, as four landmark pairs taken",
    "from the edges of the PCB itself: its left and right edges and its top and",
    "bottom edges, measured in each image by finding the outermost board pixels.",
    "The drawing's board rectangle is x 32..5658, y 122..3120 of 5810 x 3420;",
    "the photograph's is x 68..3335, y 195..1930 of 3400 x 2093.", "",
    "Four corner pairs can only produce a scale-and-shift fit, so this is a",
    "starting alignment rather than a finished one -- good to roughly a",
    "millimetre near the middle of the board and looser towards the corners,",
    "where the camera's perspective and lens distortion show. Add landmark pairs",
    "in Author Mode (Photo landmarks) on features away from the edges to let it",
    "re-solve a full projective fit; residuals are listed per landmark there."
  ],
  "layers": {
    "photo": {
      "approximate": true,
      "landmarks": [
        {
          "note": "photo corner, top left",
          "src": [-0.01181, -0.05647],
          "dst": [0.0, 0.0]
        },
        {
          "note": "photo corner, top right",
          "src": [0.99468, -0.04649],
          "dst": [1.0, 0.0]
        },
        {
          "note": "photo corner, bottom right",
          "src": [0.9931, 0.99464],
          "dst": [1.0, 1.0]
        },
        {
          "note": "photo corner, bottom left",
          "src": [-0.013, 1.00205],
          "dst": [0.0, 1.0]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "_sheetRuleComment": [
    "A18's two schematic sheets divide the board cleanly: sheet 1 is the",
    "low-voltage filter/regulator section and carries the 1..99 designators,",
    "sheet 2 is the power amplifier output supply and carries the 200-series.",
    "The reader occasionally finds a designator on the wrong sheet -- a '2' in",
    "a component value read as part of a reference -- so a placement is only",
    "kept on the sheet where that part can actually be. P901 and P902 are the",
    "exceptions: the two board connectors are drawn one per sheet.",
    "Set 'threshold' to null for an assembly whose sheets do not split this way."
  ],
  "schematicSheetRule": {
    "threshold": 200,
    "below": "sh1",
    "atOrAbove": "sh2",
    "exceptions": { "P901": "sh1", "P902": "sh2" }
  },
  "_sheetsComment": [
    "The zone grid printed around each D-size schematic sheet, used to derive a",
    "location like 'sh1/C4'. 'frame' is the inner border that bounds the zone",
    "cells, measured off sch1_full.png (6410 x 3860) at the top-left and",
    "bottom-right corners: x 32..6270, y 98..3797. Both sheets use the same",
    "drawing template, so the same frame applies to each."
  ],
  "sheets": {
    "sh1": {
      "grid": {
        "cols": ["8", "7", "6", "5", "4", "3", "2", "1"],
        "rows": ["D", "C", "B", "A"],
        "frame": { "x0": 0.005, "y0": 0.0254, "x1": 0.9781, "y1": 0.9837 }
      }
    },
    "sh2": {
      "grid": {
        "cols": ["8", "7", "6", "5", "4", "3", "2", "1"],
        "rows": ["D", "C", "B", "A"],
        "frame": { "x0": 0.005, "y0": 0.0254, "x1": 0.9781, "y1": 0.9837 }
      }
    }
  },
  "_boardComment": "x,y are the marker centre in drawing_full.png pixels. Test point rows carry row:true for the shared label/pad footprint; components carry an explicit w,h. The component entries were placed or corrected by hand in Author Mode on 2026-08-12 and exported from the browser; those carrying \"fitted\": true were later replaced by a measured body box (see _shapeComment).",
  "_shapeComment": [
    "47 entries here are the component body rather than the designator that names",
    "it, and carry \"fitted\": true to say so. A shape is only meaningful together",
    "with a body box: the reader places a marker on the lettering, and an ellipse",
    "inscribed in a 50 x 163 px rotated label is a sliver beside the part rather",
    "than a ring around it. So a circle entry is the can itself -- centre and",
    "diameter in drawing_full.png pixels, w == h -- and a rect entry with",
    "\"fitted\" is the outline, not the label.", "",
    "29 circles: 21 electrolytics, the seven fuses whose designator is printed",
    "inside the can, and U2's TO can. 18 rectangles: eight bridge rectifiers,",
    "eight of the 5 A axial diodes, K201 and S201.", "",
    "They were measured by tools/detect_round_parts.py, which casts rays out from",
    "the designator and fits a circle and a rectangle to the outline they meet,",
    "and every one was rendered on the drawing and looked at before being pasted",
    "here. What is declined is declined for a reason worth knowing:", "",
    "  C11 C12 C20 C22 C207 C208  aluminium, but drawn small enough that the",
    "                             label sits outside the circle, or with a",
    "                             broken outline -- no unique seed",
    "  F1 F2 F201-F204            designator printed clear of the can. F1 in",
    "                             particular fits a neighbouring fuse at 86%",
    "                             agreement and is rejected on containment, not",
    "                             on score. Place these by hand.",
    "  the 30 small signal diodes drawn as a symbol on a pair of leads, with no",
    "                             body outline to find at all", "",
    "Resistors are not tried by default. A --all sweep fits 31% of them, and",
    "none of those has been looked at."
  ],
